{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q86DwGReP9oHF6ww1vZ455","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-28; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\t## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n4\t- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only). Mastery:\n5\t  ONE download holding `-01.zip`..`-NN.zip` (D7 three levels deep); refs `<set zip> -> <member>`, names reused per set\n6\t  -> resolve by (set zip, member). D9: download `<id>-mastery.zip` vs refs `...-evidence-0N.zip` -> resolve by sha256\n7\t  (`lib.common.container_by_sha`). D6: two same-named downloads -> `delivery N: <zip>` refs.\n8\t\n9\tHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n10\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field.\n11\t  **D23 mutated the WHOLE carry-over kit** (values that sat constant D13-D22 re-rolled: PE/ELF arch, audio codec, video\n12\t  dims, Mach-O became FAT, zip CD order shuffled) -- every carried extractor must parse the general case, not D-day's sample.\n13\t- Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password). D1-7: one tiny member, one fact; D8-9: cumulative kit in\n14\t  every mode; D10-14: one field everywhere. **D15+ split the modes**: single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative\n15\t  kit (D15 20 -> D28 33 fields, +1/day), Mastery = N kits x the TT set (N=5 to D21, then +1/day: 11 D27, 12 D28), incl. a\n16\t  cross-member \"synthesis\" question. Pre-arm EVERY earlier family AND the synthesis before the timed run.\n17\t- Member families (one per day, each lasting ONE day as the single's field, then carried in the timed kit): note ->\n18\t  jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE (D9-11) -> .NET (D12) -> MSI -> LNK -> OOXML -> `.eml` -> WAV -> MP4 -> ELF\n19\t  (D19) -> Mach-O -> APK -> JAR -> SQLite (D23) -> EVTX -> regf hive -> Prefetch (D24-26 Windows DFIR: structure walk,\n20\t  pointer follow, decompress-then-parse) -> PCAP (D27, network) -> raw GPT DISK image `disk-001.img` (D28: one layer\n21\t  DOWN, the container of every earlier family). Member name `<family>-001.<ext>`.\n22\t- fmt word = the DOMAIN, read it from the question: `email` (not eml), `media` (audio D17 AND video D18, ffprobe\n23\t  vocabulary), `registry` (not regf), `disk` (raw image, not vhd), else the plain format (`pe` `msi` `lnk` `elf` `macho`\n24\t  `apk` `jar` `sqlite` `evtx` `prefetch` `pcap`). Question `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`; id\n25\t  `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`), `dNN` = the family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` only for\n26\t  media (`d17-audio-001-media-`). Field = the spec struct's name (full list in \"Day by day\").\n27\t- Flavor text promises extra findings that are NEVER asked (D19-D28 every day: fleets, clones, nested launchers,\n28\t  \"truncated, embedded, impossible claim\", \"selectively shortened timeline\", \"planted hive\", \"connect traces to hosts\",\n29\t  \"reject malformed captures\", D28 \"locate evidence by offset, prove which image was rebuilt from an incomplete\n30\t  source\"). Graded = the STRUCTURAL truth; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Titles pun on the field\n31\t  (D19 \"Little Endian\" = EI_DATA; D20 \"Universal Appeal\" = fat; D22 \"Main Character Energy\" = Main-Class; D24 \"Event\n32\t  Horizon\" = record count; D25 \"Hive Mind\" = root key; D26 \"Before You Go\" = Prefetch; D27 \"Packet Loss Prevention\" =\n33\t  packet COUNT; D28 \"Where It All Began\" = partition START LBA). Flavor depth shows up as TIMED mutations, not fields.\n34\t- Singles: D1-9 ~27-60 s; one convention submit lost D10, D13, D15, D20; two D16. Prebuilt race HITS: D18 ~5 s, D19\n35\t  ~13, D22 ~19, D23 ~29, D26 ~29, D27 ~22 s. MISSES -> live worker: D17 ~24, D21 ~32, D24 ~21, D25 ~17 (`registry` vs\n36\t  `regf`), D28 ~22 s (`disk` vs `gpt`). TT/Mastery: CORRECT every day; D15-17 + D19 after a generalize (synthesis\n37\t  dispatch); D23 after one wrong TT submit (list ORDER); since D24 first try in seconds (D28: TT 33 fields 3.2 s,\n38\t  Mastery 396 = 12 sets 4.3 s).\n39\t\n40\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n41\t- **Delivery layout** -- names drift: D1-14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`; D15+ TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery\n42\t  `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..NN.zip` (see \"Question-text tags / nesting\"). Route by the ref's text before\n43\t  `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.\n44\t- **Field-set / set count** -- D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 1/20/100 ... D21 1/26/130\n45\t  (+1 field/day); D22 1/27/162 (6 sets); D23 1/28/196 (7 sets); D24 1/29/232 (8 sets); D25 1/30/270 (9 sets); D26\n46\t  1/31/310 (10 sets -- `set10.` sorts before `set2.` as a string: order sets numerically); D27 1/32/352 (11 sets);\n47\t  D28 1/33/396 (12 sets).\n48\t  Enumerate `setN.` prefixes from the live ids. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg` `d05-png` `d06-pdf` `d07-zip` (eocd,\n49\t  CD names) `d09-pe` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename) `d12-dotnet` `d13-msi` `d14-lnk` `d15-ooxml` `d16-email` `d17-audio` `d18-video` `d19-elf`\n50\t  `d20-macho` `d21-apk` `d22-jar` `d23-sqlite` `d24-evtx` `d25-registry` `d26-prefetch` `d27-pcap` `d28-disk` + synthesis.\n51\t  Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX (reference solver answering all 33: `challenges/day28/metadata-where-it-all-began/solver/solve.py`; lane seed `local_answer` +\n52\t  `synthesis_answer` + lib.meta).\n53\t- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family** -- D16 `email` (lib `eml`), D17/18 `media` (ids `d17-audio-`/`d18-video-`),\n54\t  D19 `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`, D20 `macho.cpu_type_set`, D21 `apk.package_name`, D22 `jar.main_class`, D23\n55\t  `sqlite.page_size_bytes`, D24 `evtx.record_count`, D25 `registry.hive_root_name` (lib `regf.root_key_name` -> MISS),\n56\t  D26 `prefetch.executable_name` (HIT), D27 `pcap.packet_count` (HIT), D28 `disk.partition_start_lba_sequence` (lib\n57\t  `disk` = virtual-disk containers; GPT walk only under `gpt`/`mbr`/`partition_table`.`partition_start_lbas` -> MISS).\n58\t  Vocabulary = the home tool (ffprobe, capinfos, sfdisk) or the spec struct; header codes ALWAYS raw `0x` hex. Rule:\n59\t  take `<fmt>.<field>` from the question (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`~`eml`/`mime`;\n60\t  `media`~`audio`/`video`/`av`; `jar`~`war`; `sqlite`~`db`; `evtx`~`evt`/`eventlog`; `registry`~`regf`/`hive`;\n61\t  `prefetch`~`pf`/`scca`; `pcap`~`pcapng`/`capture`; `disk`~`gpt`/`mbr`/`partition_table`/`image`) and field synonyms\n62\t  (`_sequence`~`_list`/plural `s`), route the extractor by MAGIC + member names, fall back to the field under any fmt.\n63\t- **Member values (D23+: EVERYTHING re-rolls every day)** -- never cache across sets/modes. Seen: identity sizes\n64\t  72-378 B (CRLF/LF, BOM in some sets), PDF `1.0`-`2.0`, zip entries 2-13, PE Machine (`0x014c` `0x8664` `0xaa64`\n65\t  `0x01c0/2/4` `0x01f0` `0x0ebc` `0x5064` `0x0266`), audio under `audio-001.wav` (`pcm_s16le` `mp3` `opus` `vorbis`\n66\t  `aac` M4A, `flac`), ELF e_machine (`0x003e` `0x0003` `0x0028` `0x002b` `0x0102` `0x0016` `0x00b7` `0x00f3`), Mach-O\n67\t  thin (LE-32/64) or FAT 2-3 slices, Main-Class 1-4 parts, SQLite page 512-65536, EVTX 3-119 records (one chunk),\n68\t  regf root `[A-Za-z0-9]{6,32}`, Prefetch WRAPPER flips (D26 single `MAM\\x04` Xpress-Huffman, timed plain SCCA v30),\n69\t  PCAP classic v2.4 only (LE-us / LE-ns `4d 3c b2 a1` / BE-us `a1 b2 c3 d4`; linktype 1/101/105/147; 3-39 records,\n70\t  snapped ones count), DISK (D28, 14 images): protective MBR `ee` + GPT rev 1.0, 512-B sectors, entries @LBA2 128x128,\n71\t  valid CRCs, backup hdr at the last LBA, 61-582 KiB, 1-6 used entries contiguous from slot 0, starts 34-367, table\n72\t  order == ascending, names `<word><digit>`, partitions ALL ZERO (no FS, no MBR-only/EBR/4Kn yet). Rule: decode the\n73\t  general structure (byte order from the file, every slice/chunk/entry, follow every offset, decompress any wrapper\n74\t  by its magic), never the D-day sample's constant.\n75\t- **List ORDER under mutation (D23)** -- D8-D22 zips stored CD entries already sorted; D23 shuffled the CD and the GM\n76\t  REJECTED CD order, accepted ascending sort; fat Mach-O slices ascending `0x%08x` (fat_arch order rejected). Rule:\n77\t  `_names`/`_set`/`_targets` = sorted ascending + deduped (string sort of the emitted spelling); EXCEPT synthesis\n78\t  (digest order) and `_sequence`/\"in order\" fields (D28: partition-TABLE order -- integers, NEVER string-sorted:\n79\t  `[86,117]` string-sorts to `[117,86]`). Always `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"))` -- never `str()` a list.\n80\t- **Identity member roster** (D15+) -- `evidence-note*.txt`, `evidence-note-copy*.txt`, `roster*.csv` (timed names\n81\t  may carry `-<6hex>`; ids keep the bare stem): ids `<stem>-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,\n82\t  text-utf8-bom-present}`; filename artifact = the container only -> map the stem by PREFIX. Sets may lack a member\n83\t  (D25) or ask a DIFFERENT 7 of the 21 identity ids (D26+) -- answer exactly the ids each set lists.\n84\t- **Synthesis / cross-member** (D15+) -- id `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order` (TODAY's NN), kind `json`, norm\n85\t  `case_insensitive`, \"Compute the full-file SHA-256 digest of each named file, then submit a compact JSON array of\n86\t  their filenames in ascending digest order. Files: [...]\". Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, hash each under the\n87\t  ref's container, sort by hex digest -- `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo)`, get_bytes bound\n88\t  INSIDE the per-set worker. Shape: note + re-picked kit members + TODAY's member; 4 names D15-20, FIVE D21-26, SIX\n89\t  D27-28 (D28 TT note/png/msi/mp4/sqlite/img) -- never assume a length. The list differs between the 409 contract\n90\t  and the live attempt AND between sets of one Mastery -- parse each set's own text. Only sha256 seen.\n91\t- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version, regf FileName\n92\t  @0x30): answer from the structure the field names; `elf.*` of an `MZ` member = `none`.\n93\t- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex `trim` only -> lowercase),\n94\t  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (compact array; `*_set`/`*_names`/`*_sequence` = a list even with ONE element).\n95\t- **Question-text tags / nesting** -- D9 ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]` suffix, D15+ ``Inspect `<member>`. ``\n96\t  prefix: strip, route by id + `artifact`. The asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (D7): resolve by the name after `->`;\n97\t  OOXML/APK/JAR members ARE zips -- parse them as the member. Mastery: ONE download of `-01..-NN.zip`, refs `<set zip>\n98\t  -> <member>`, names reused per set; download vs ref names may differ (D9) -> `lib.common.container_by_sha`.\n99\t\n100\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n101\t| You see | First move |\n102\t|---|---|\n103\t| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | python `zipfile` read of the member in memory (`7z l -slt` for orientation) |\n104\t| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the member bytes; the id stem names WHICH member |\n105\t| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n106\t| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`) -> `true`/`false` |\n107\t| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width |\n108\t| `png.ihdr_*` | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n109\t| `zip.eocd_*` | of the NAMED zip: last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+10 total entries, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 (`PK\\x06\\x07` -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32) |\n110\t| `zip.central_directory_*` | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from cd offset: name len @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name @+46. Raw stored paths, then SORT ascending (D23: CD order REJECTED); UTF-8 if flag 0x800 else cp437 |\n111\t| `pdf.header_version` | `head -c 16 f | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; catalog `/Version` is a diagnostic only |\n112\t| `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4 (any IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_*, D23 saw 7 values); OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |\n113\t| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |\n114\t| `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n115\t| `elf.*` (`7f 45 4c 46`) | EI_CLASS @4 (1=32, 2=64), EI_DATA @5 (1=LSB `<`, 2=MSB `>`) picks the byte order for EVERYTHING after @16: e_type u16 @16, e_machine u16 @18, e_entry @24. `xxd -s 16 -l 4 f` + `readelf -h f`. `lib.meta` fmt `elf` |\n116\t| `macho.*` (`cf fa ed fe` LE-64, `ce fa ed fe` LE-32, `fe ed fa ce/cf` BE; fat `ca fe ba be` / fat64 `ca fe ba bf`, always BE) | thin: cputype u32 @4 (byte order from the magic). Fat: nfat_arch u32 @4, then 20-B (fat64 32-B) fat_arch {cputype, cpusubtype, offset, size, align}; Java class shares `cafebabe` (major @6 >= 45). `cpu_type_set` = JSON list `\"0x%08x\"`, deduped, SORTED ascending (D23 fat 2-3 slices). `lib.meta` fmt `macho` |\n117\t| `apk.*` / `.apk` (`PK` + `AndroidManifest.xml` + `classes.dex`) | manifest is BINARY AXML (`03 00 08 00`): `aapt dump badging f.apk \\| head -1`; stdlib `lib/meta/apk.py manifest_attr(axml, 'manifest', 'package')`. Triage routes APKs to `$mobile-android` -- ignore it |\n118\t| `jar.*` / `.jar/.war/.ear` (`PK` + `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`) | `unzip -p f.jar META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` (CRLF, 72-B lines, ONE-space continuations); main section up to the first blank line; `Main-Class` verbatim. Spring Boot: `Start-Class` = app. `lib/meta/prebuilt/jar.py` |\n119\t| `sqlite.*` / `.sqlite/.db/.sqlite3` (`SQLite format 3\\0` @0) | 100-B header, BIG-endian: page size u16 @16 (`1` = 65536), write/read ver @18/@19 (2 = WAL), file change counter @24, in-header db size (pages) @28, freelist @32/@36, encoding u32 @56 (1 UTF-8, 2 UTF-16le, 3 UTF-16be), user_version @60, application_id @68, version-valid-for @92, SQLITE_VERSION_NUMBER @96. `xxd -s 16 -l 2 f`; `file f` prints the summary; `sqlite3 f 'PRAGMA page_size'`. In-window `lib/meta/prebuilt/sqlite.py` (header + stdlib sqlite_master walk + browser history) |\n120\t| `evtx.*` / `.evtx` (`ElfFile\\0` @0, `ElfChnk\\0` @0x1000) | LE everywhere. File header: next_record_id u64 @24, chunk count u16 @42, version @36/@38 (3.2), flags u32 @120 (1 dirty, 2 full). Each 64 KiB chunk: first/last record number @8/@16, ids @24/@32, free-space offset u32 @48; records `2a 2a 00 00` from chunk+0x200, size u32 @+4, EventRecordID u64 @+8, FILETIME @+16. `record_count` = walk EVERY chunk's records up to its free offset (D24); `file f` prints chunks + next record no.; python-evtx `Evtx.Evtx` (worker-only). `lib/meta/prebuilt/evtx.py` |\n121\t| `registry.*` / `regf.*` / `.hiv` `NTUSER.DAT` `SYSTEM` (`regf` @0) | base block 4 KiB LE: seq1/seq2 u32 @4/@8, last written FILETIME @12, ver @20/@24 (1.3), root cell off u32 @0x24 (rel. to 0x1000), bins size @0x28, FileName UTF-16 @0x30 (64 B; DECOY for the root). Cell = i32 size (neg = used) + `nk`: flags u16 @+2 (0x20 COMP_NAME -> latin-1 else UTF-16LE; 0x04 HIVE_ENTRY = root), FILETIME @+4, subkeys @+0x14, list off @+0x1c, values @+0x24, value list @+0x28, name len u16 @+0x48, name @+0x4c (offsets after the size). `hive_root_name` = root nk name verbatim (D25). `xxd -s $((0x1000+root)) -l 128`; regipy (worker-only) |\n122\t| `prefetch.*` / `.pf` (`SCCA` @4, version u32 @0: 17/23/26/30/31; `MAM` @0 = Win10+ compressed) | `MAM` + type byte (low nibble 4 = Xpress-Huffman; 0x80 = CRC32 u32 follows), uncompressed size u32 @4, stream @8 (@12 with CRC) -> decompress FIRST. SCCA: file size u32 @12, exe name UTF-16LE @16 (60 B, NUL-terminated), path hash u32 @0x4C; run count / 8 last-run FILETIMEs / volumes per version. `.venv` `dissect.util.compression.lzxpress_huffman.decompress(b[8:])` (worker), `lib/meta/prebuilt/prefetch.py` (pure-Python, in-window) |\n123\t| `pcap.*` / `.pcap` `.cap` (`d4 c3 b2 a1` LE-us, `4d 3c b2 a1` LE-ns, `a1 b2 c3 d4` / `a1 b2 3c 4d` BE; pcapng `0a 0d 0d 0a`) | byte order FROM THE MAGIC; 24-B global hdr: ver u16 @4/@6 (2.4), snaplen u32 @16, linktype u32 @20; records = 16-B hdr {ts_sec, ts_frac, incl_len @+8, orig_len @+12} + incl_len bytes -> `packet_count` = complete records walked (D27). pcapng: walk blocks {type u32, len u32 ... len}, SHB `0a0d0d0a` BOM `1a2b3c4d` @8 sets order per section, count EPB 6 / SPB 3 / OPB 2. `capinfos -M f` / `tshark -r f \\| wc -l` cross-check; `lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap.py` |\n124\t| `disk.*` / `gpt.*` / `mbr.*` / `.img` `.dd` `.raw` `.001` (`55 aa` @0x1FE; `EFI PART` @512 or @4096) | protective MBR type `ee` @0x1C2 -> GPT: entry LBA u64 @hdr+72, count u32 @+80, size u32 @+84; each entry {type GUID 16, unique 16, first LBA u64 @+32, last @+40, attrs @+48, name UTF-16LE @+56}; skip all-zero type GUID; keep TABLE order (D28 `partition_start_lba_sequence` = JSON ints). No GPT -> MBR 4x16 B @0x1BE {type @+4, start u32 @+8, count @+12}, types 05/0f/85 -> walk the EBR chain (logical start = EBR LBA + rel). `sfdisk -d f.img` / `fdisk -l f.img` / `sgdisk -p f.img` / `mmls f.img` cross-check. In-window: `lib/meta/prebuilt/vbr.py` (`gpt`/`mbr` fmts) + the D28 solver's `disk_partition_starts` |\n125\t| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |\n126\t| `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property`. `olefile` in venv |\n127\t| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |\n128\t| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` in EVERY `*.rels` part; `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; sorted |\n129\t| `email.*` / `.eml` | `grep -ai '^message-id' f.eml`; `lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(data, {\"field\": f})`. Values VERBATIM (Message-ID keeps `<...>`) |\n130\t| `media.*` audio (`RIFF..WAVE`, `ID3`/`ff fb`, `OggS`, `fLaC`, `ftyp`, `1a 45 df a3`, `FORM..AIFF`) | route by MAGIC (D23 TT/Mastery: WAV, MP3, Ogg Opus, Ogg Vorbis all appeared under `audio-001.*`). WAV tag -> FFmpeg names (Conventions); Ogg: first packet `OpusHead` -> `opus`, `\\x01vorbis` -> `vorbis`. Truth: bundled `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` |\n131\t| `media.*video*` / MP4-MOV (`....ftyp`), MKV/WebM, AVI | box walk `moov` -> first `trak` whose `mdia/hdlr` = `vide` -> `stsd` entry: w,h u16 BE @entry+32; cross-check tkhd, SPS crop. `lib.meta` fmt `media` |\n132\t| `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |\n133\t| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |\n134\t| exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |\n135\t| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"mislabeled\", \"embedded\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0 of the NAMED member; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n136\t| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(sorted(v), separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` unless the field is an order (synthesis, `_sequence`); integer lists stay ints |\n137\t| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |\n138\t\n139\t## Day by day\n140\t**Days 1-14** (one field each, all timed first try): D1 identity -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16` -> D3 BOM -> D4 JPEG SOFn\n141\t`<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR -> D6 `pdf.header_version` `x.y` -> D7 `zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip -> D8 CD names\n142\t(compact JSON; disk order happened to be sorted) -> D9-11 one Go PE: `coff_machine_u16_hex` `0x014c`, entry RVA\n143\t`0x%08x` (unpadded REJECTED), `version_original_filename` verbatim -> D12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le)`\n144\tlowercase, no braces) -> D13 `msi.product_code_guid` (stored WITH braces; brace-less REJECTED) -> D14 `lnk.target_path_windows`.\n145\t\n146\t**Days 15-27** (single = 1 new-family field; TT/Mastery = cumulative kit + synthesis): D15 `ooxml.external_relationship_\n147\ttargets` (rels `TargetMode=\"External\"` Targets SORTED; rels order REJECTED). D16 `email.message_id` (VERBATIM with `<>`;\n148\t2 lost: id regex -> `none`, stripped brackets). D17 `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (WAV PCM16 -> `pcm_s16le`). D18\n149\t`media.primary_video_dimensions` (first `vide` trak stsd -> `320x180`). D19 \"Little Endian\" `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`\n150\t(@18 in EI_DATA order -> `0x003e`). D20 \"Universal Appeal\" `macho.cpu_type_set` (THIN arm64 -> `[\"0x0100000c\"]`;\n151\t`[\"arm64\"]` REJECTED). D21 \"Package Deal\" `apk.package_name` (binary-AXML `<manifest package=>` verbatim, NOT\n152\t`android:label`). D22 \"Main Character Energy\" `jar.main_class` (MANIFEST.MF `Main-Class` verbatim, dotted, no\n153\t`.class`). D23 \"Page Me Maybe\" `sqlite.page_size_bytes` (u16 BE @16, `1` = 65536; timed kit MUTATED for the first\n154\ttime -> 1 wrong TT submit on CD-order names). D24 \"Event Horizon\" `evtx.record_count` (walk `**\\0\\0` records of EVERY\n155\tchunk to its free-space offset u32 @48; live struct walk ~21 s). D25 \"Hive Mind\" `registry.hive_root_name` (base block\n156\tu32 @0x24 -> nk @0x1000+off+4 -> name len u16 @+0x48, name @+0x4c, ASCII if flag 0x20; base-block FileName @0x30 =\n157\t\"renamed\" DECOY; race MISS on fmt word, live ~17 s). D26 \"Before You Go\" `prefetch.executable_name` (single `MAM\\x04`\n158\tXpress-Huffman -> SCCA v30, exe UTF-16LE @16 to NUL, uppercase `CMD.EXE`; timed plain SCCA; race hit ~29 s). D27 \"Packet\n159\tLoss Prevention\" `pcap.packet_count` (24-B global hdr, then 16-B rec hdrs by incl_len @+8 to EOF; byte order + us/ns\n160\tfrom the magic; snapped records count; prebuilt race hit ~22 s). Timed D15-17 + D19: synthesis dispatch missing ->\n161\tgeneralize; D18, D20-22, D24-27 first try.\n162\t\n163\t**Day 28 — Where It All Began** (`disk.partition_start_lba_sequence`, kind `json` \"compact valid JSON array with exact\n164\tvalues and order\", norm `trim`, id `d28-disk-001-disk-partition-start-lba-sequence`). Prompt: \"Disk images hold every\n165\tprevious artifact family in context. Recover partition layouts, locate evidence by offset, and prove which image was\n166\trebuilt from an incomplete source.\" Title pun = where each partition BEGINS (start LBA) / LBA 0, where a disk begins.\n167\t- Artifact: `metadata-day-28-evidence.zip` (606 B) -> `disk-001.img` (131 072 B = 256 sectors): protective MBR (one\n168\t  `ee` entry), GPT header `EFI PART` @512 (rev 1.0, hdr 92 B, CRCs valid), entry array @LBA2 (128 x 128 B), backup\n169\t  header at LBA 255; ONE used entry, Microsoft basic data, name `HUNTRESS EVIDENCE`, LBAs 34-222 -> answer `[34]`.\n170\t  Partition bytes all zero: the flavor's \"every previous artifact family\", \"locate evidence by offset\" and \"rebuilt\n171\t  from an incomplete source\" were NOT asked in any mode (as every day since D19).\n172\t- Insight: GPT wins over the MBR when MBR slot 0 type is `ee` and `EFI PART` sits at LBA1; read the header's own entry\n173\t  LBA/count/size (never hard-code 2/128/128), skip zero type-GUID entries, emit first_lba u64 @+32 per entry in TABLE\n174\t  order as compact JSON integers (not strings, not byte offsets). MBR fallback incl. the EBR chain is in the solver.\n175\t- Tools: `xxd -s 0x1be -l 66 f.img` (protective `ee`), `xxd -s 512 -l 92`, `xxd -s 1024 -l 128`; `sfdisk -d f.img` /\n176\t  `fdisk -l` cross-check; ~25-line python `struct` walk (`disk_partition_starts` in the day's solver).\n177\t- Time: GM CORRECT ~22 s after start, 0 wrong. Race MISS: lib had the GPT walk (`vbr.py`) but under fmts\n178\t  `gpt`/`mbr`/`partition_table` with field `partition_start_lbas`, and lib's `disk` fmt = virtual-disk containers\n179\t  (VHD/VMDK/QCOW2) -> live worker added `local_answer`. TT 33 fields 3.2 s (solve 0.9) + Mastery 396 = TWELVE sets\n180\t  4.3 s (solve 2.1), first submit, no generalize. Timed images varied only in size / entry count (1-6) / start LBAs.\n181\t\n182\t## GM answer conventions learned\n183\t- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes/counts: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, any\n184\t  case. Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n185\t- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR, video D18): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase `x`; video = ffprobe v:0 coded size.\n186\t- PDF header version: bare `x.y` (absent -> `none`, unconfirmed). `_bytes` sizes = decoded integer (`1` -> `65536`, D23).\n187\t  `evtx.record_count` = records actually present (chunk walk, D24); `pcap.packet_count` = complete libpcap records\n188\t  walked (D27; snapped incl_len < orig_len records count; pcapng = EPB+SPB+OPB, unverified).\n189\t- Stored strings VERBATIM (no quotes, case kept, delimiters kept): PE StringFileInfo (D11), LNK LinkInfo path (D14),\n190\t  OOXML Target URL (D15), Message-ID WITH `<>` (D16), manifest `package` (D21), `Main-Class` (D22), registry ROOT nk\n191\t  name (D25: no leading `\\`, no `HKEY_*`, not the base-block FileName), Prefetch SCCA header exe name (D26: UTF-16LE\n192\t  @16 to the first NUL, uppercase as stored, `.EXE` kept, no path, not the `.pf` filename stem / `-HASH`).\n193\t- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces, values SORTED ascending: `zip.central_directory_member_names`\n194\t  (D23 CD order REJECTED), `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` (D15 rels order REJECTED), `macho.cpu_type_set`\n195\t  (`\"0x%08x\"`, deduped). ORDER fields: `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` = names by hex digest ascending; D28\n196\t  `disk.partition_start_lba_sequence` = JSON INTEGERS (sectors, not bytes, not quoted: `[34]`, `[60,93,148]`) in\n197\t  partition-TABLE order (== ascending in all 14 D28 images, so table-vs-sorted is untested; `_sequence` reads as table order).\n198\t- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width (u16 `0x014c`\n199\t  `0x003e`, u32 `0x00065bd0`, Mach-O `0x0100000c` even without `_hex`). Width from the STRUCT / `_uNN_`; value in the\n200\t  file's own byte order. (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; the binary lane wants `i386` -- different generator.)\n201\t- GUIDs follow the source: .NET MVID lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode stored string uppercase WITH braces (D13).\n202\t- Media codec names: ffprobe `codec_name` (WAV tag 1 -> `pcm_u8`/`pcm_s16le`/`pcm_s24le`/`pcm_s32le` by bits, 3\n203\t  `pcm_f32le`, 6 `pcm_alaw`, 7 `pcm_mulaw`, 0x55 `mp3`; MP3 `mp3`; Ogg `opus`/`vorbis` -- all GM-accepted).\n204\t- Rejected: `0x65bd0` (D10 unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-order targets (D15); bracket-less Message-ID\n205\t  (D16); `[\"arm64\"]` (D20); CD-order names (D23); Python repr `['a', 'b']` for any json (D23).\n206\t- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_`, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim, `e_machine`,\n207\t  `page_size`, libscca `executable_name`) -- read it literally to pick the structure; header CODES are raw `0x` hex.\n208\t\n209\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n210\t- **Carry-over mutation (D23, 1 wrong TT submit + a Mastery generalize)**: an extractor that only ever saw one sample\n211\t  value is untested. Before a timed run, ask of every carried field \"what if this is the multi-element / other-endian\n212\t  / other-codec / compressed-or-not case?\" -- fat Mach-O, shuffled CD, Ogg audio, non-x86 machines arrived the same day.\n213\t- **json list output**: sort + compact `json.dumps` at ONE choke point (D23 Mastery: a local Python list got `str()`'d).\n214\t- **Synthesis dispatch** (lost D15-17, D19): start the day's solver from the lane seed (`local_answer` +\n215\t  `synthesis_answer` -> `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, artifacts root set INSIDE `_solve_pairs`; one process/set).\n216\t- **Registry misses** (D14 suffix, D16 `eml`/`email`, D17 `wav`/`media`, D21 no `apk`, D25 `regf.root_key_name` vs\n217\t  `registry.hive_root_name`, D28 fmt-word COLLISION: lib `disk` = VHD/VMDK/QCOW2 detector, GM `disk` = raw GPT image,\n218\t  the GPT walk lived under `gpt`/`mbr` -- a fmt hit is not enough, its detector must accept today's MAGIC): grep the\n219\t  lib for the field's last words (`start_lba`, `partition`) under EVERY fmt --\n220\t  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"` + grep\n221\t  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py`. Shape trap (D20): `cpu_type_set` hit scalar `cpu_type` -- `_set`/`_list`/`_names` = a list.\n222\t- Unwired template (D22) / id slugs (D16, 1 wrong): `--from-solver` before today's field is dispatched emits `none`;\n223\t  ids repeat the fmt word (`d16-email-001-email-message-id`) -> anchor `-\\d+-<fmt>-(.+)$`. `none` = absent in the\n224\t  bytes, never \"my parser returned None\".\n225\t- Format traps: byte order from the file (ELF EI_DATA @5, Mach-O / PCAP magic; fat headers + SQLite ALWAYS BE,\n226\t  MBR/GPT ALWAYS LE); fat cputype = fat_arch; video geometry has 4 sources (trust SPS-cropped); EVTX count = WALK\n227\t  each chunk to its free offset; regf cell offsets are relative to 0x1000 + an i32 size; SQLite `1` = 65536; Prefetch:\n228\t  test `MAM` @0 BEFORE `SCCA` @4 (wrapper flips between modes); GPT: entry LBA/count/size come from the HEADER, sector\n229\t  size 512 or 4096 (probe `EFI PART` at both), unused entries = zero type GUID, protective `ee` says nothing else.\n230\t- A pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the 409 `start_required` body (questions, NO `answer_ids`; Files lists\n231\t  and member numbering differ from the live attempt); answer under the live ids. The flavor never widens the field.\n232\t- Container-of-containers: a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` reads the OUTER EOCD -- resolve the named member first.\n233\t  Decoys (`*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF): bytes win; require the format's magic (else `none`).\n234\t- Timed windows are seconds, mostly GM round-trips (D23 Mastery start 3.2 + download 2.2 + solve 1.3 + submit 2.4 s;\n235\t  D26 Mastery download 6.8 MB / 9 s). Parse in memory, never shell out in-window; decompress each member once.\n236\t- Tools: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost, mediainfo,\n237\t  sqlite3, ImageMagick, readelf/objdump, aapt + apktool/jadx (`source bin/env.sh`); .venv: olevba/oleid, olefile,\n238\t  pefile, pyelftools, LnkParse3, dnfile, mutagen, androguard, python-evtx, regipy, dissect.util (lzxpress_huffman,\n239\t  lznt1, lz4, lzo) -- all worker-only, not in the prebuild gate; disks: sfdisk/fdisk/sgdisk/gdisk/partx, TSK\n240\t  `mmls`/`fsstat`/`fls`/`icat`, qemu-img (NOT parted, ewfinfo, pytsk3, dissect.volume); msitools under tools/msitools; ffmpeg 7.0.2 at\n241\t  `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2` (not on PATH). NOT: ffprobe, sox.\n242\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed430d07-8f66-4813-9978-3741f4f448f4","uuid":"70169b21-2d82-4462-a24b-bc265f1cbbff","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:39:55.760Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md","content":"# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-28; updated after every day)\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only). Mastery:\n  ONE download holding `-01.zip`..`-NN.zip` (D7 three levels deep); refs `<set zip> -> <member>`, names reused per set\n  -> resolve by (set zip, member). D9: download `<id>-mastery.zip` vs refs `...-evidence-0N.zip` -> resolve by sha256\n  (`lib.common.container_by_sha`). D6: two same-named downloads -> `delivery N: <zip>` refs.\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field.\n  **D23 mutated the WHOLE carry-over kit** (values that sat constant D13-D22 re-rolled: PE/ELF arch, audio codec, video\n  dims, Mach-O became FAT, zip CD order shuffled) -- every carried extractor must parse the general case, not D-day's sample.\n- Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password). D1-7: one tiny member, one fact; D8-9: cumulative kit in\n  every mode; D10-14: one field everywhere. **D15+ split the modes**: single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative\n  kit (D15 20 -> D28 33 fields, +1/day), Mastery = N kits x the TT set (N=5 to D21, then +1/day: 11 D27, 12 D28), incl. a\n  cross-member \"synthesis\" question. Pre-arm EVERY earlier family AND the synthesis before the timed run.\n- Member families (one per day, each lasting ONE day as the single's field, then carried in the timed kit): note ->\n  jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE (D9-11) -> .NET (D12) -> MSI -> LNK -> OOXML -> `.eml` -> WAV -> MP4 -> ELF\n  (D19) -> Mach-O -> APK -> JAR -> SQLite (D23) -> EVTX -> regf hive -> Prefetch (D24-26 Windows DFIR: structure walk,\n  pointer follow, decompress-then-parse) -> PCAP (D27, network) -> raw GPT DISK image `disk-001.img` (D28: one layer\n  DOWN, the container of every earlier family). Member name `<family>-001.<ext>`.\n- fmt word = the DOMAIN, read it from the question: `email` (not eml), `media` (audio D17 AND video D18, ffprobe\n  vocabulary), `registry` (not regf), `disk` (raw image, not vhd), else the plain format (`pe` `msi` `lnk` `elf` `macho`\n  `apk` `jar` `sqlite` `evtx` `prefetch` `pcap`). Question `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`; id\n  `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`), `dNN` = the family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` only for\n  media (`d17-audio-001-media-`). Field = the spec struct's name (full list in \"Day by day\").\n- Flavor text promises extra findings that are NEVER asked (D19-D28 every day: fleets, clones, nested launchers,\n  \"truncated, embedded, impossible claim\", \"selectively shortened timeline\", \"planted hive\", \"connect traces to hosts\",\n  \"reject malformed captures\", D28 \"locate evidence by offset, prove which image was rebuilt from an incomplete\n  source\"). Graded = the STRUCTURAL truth; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Titles pun on the field\n  (D19 \"Little Endian\" = EI_DATA; D20 \"Universal Appeal\" = fat; D22 \"Main Character Energy\" = Main-Class; D24 \"Event\n  Horizon\" = record count; D25 \"Hive Mind\" = root key; D26 \"Before You Go\" = Prefetch; D27 \"Packet Loss Prevention\" =\n  packet COUNT; D28 \"Where It All Began\" = partition START LBA). Flavor depth shows up as TIMED mutations, not fields.\n- Singles: D1-9 ~27-60 s; one convention submit lost D10, D13, D15, D20; two D16. Prebuilt race HITS: D18 ~5 s, D19\n  ~13, D22 ~19, D23 ~29, D26 ~29, D27 ~22 s. MISSES -> live worker: D17 ~24, D21 ~32, D24 ~21, D25 ~17 (`registry` vs\n  `regf`), D28 ~22 s (`disk` vs `gpt`). TT/Mastery: CORRECT every day; D15-17 + D19 after a generalize (synthesis\n  dispatch); D23 after one wrong TT submit (list ORDER); since D24 first try in seconds (D28: TT 33 fields 3.2 s,\n  Mastery 396 = 12 sets 4.3 s).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- names drift: D1-14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`; D15+ TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery\n  `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..NN.zip` (see \"Question-text tags / nesting\"). Route by the ref's text before\n  `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.\n- **Field-set / set count** -- D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 1/20/100 ... D21 1/26/130\n  (+1 field/day); D22 1/27/162 (6 sets); D23 1/28/196 (7 sets); D24 1/29/232 (8 sets); D25 1/30/270 (9 sets); D26\n  1/31/310 (10 sets -- `set10.` sorts before `set2.` as a string: order sets numerically); D27 1/32/352 (11 sets);\n  D28 1/33/396 (12 sets).\n  Enumerate `setN.` prefixes from the live ids. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg` `d05-png` `d06-pdf` `d07-zip` (eocd,\n  CD names) `d09-pe` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename) `d12-dotnet` `d13-msi` `d14-lnk` `d15-ooxml` `d16-email` `d17-audio` `d18-video` `d19-elf`\n  `d20-macho` `d21-apk` `d22-jar` `d23-sqlite` `d24-evtx` `d25-registry` `d26-prefetch` `d27-pcap` `d28-disk` + synthesis.\n  Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX (reference solver answering all 33: `challenges/day28/metadata-where-it-all-began/solver/solve.py`; lane seed `local_answer` +\n  `synthesis_answer` + lib.meta).\n- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family** -- D16 `email` (lib `eml`), D17/18 `media` (ids `d17-audio-`/`d18-video-`),\n  D19 `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`, D20 `macho.cpu_type_set`, D21 `apk.package_name`, D22 `jar.main_class`, D23\n  `sqlite.page_size_bytes`, D24 `evtx.record_count`, D25 `registry.hive_root_name` (lib `regf.root_key_name` -> MISS),\n  D26 `prefetch.executable_name` (HIT), D27 `pcap.packet_count` (HIT), D28 `disk.partition_start_lba_sequence` (lib\n  `disk` = virtual-disk containers; GPT walk only under `gpt`/`mbr`/`partition_table`.`partition_start_lbas` -> MISS).\n  Vocabulary = the home tool (ffprobe, capinfos, sfdisk) or the spec struct; header codes ALWAYS raw `0x` hex. Rule:\n  take `<fmt>.<field>` from the question (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`~`eml`/`mime`;\n  `media`~`audio`/`video`/`av`; `jar`~`war`; `sqlite`~`db`; `evtx`~`evt`/`eventlog`; `registry`~`regf`/`hive`;\n  `prefetch`~`pf`/`scca`; `pcap`~`pcapng`/`capture`; `disk`~`gpt`/`mbr`/`partition_table`/`image`) and field synonyms\n  (`_sequence`~`_list`/plural `s`), route the extractor by MAGIC + member names, fall back to the field under any fmt.\n- **Member values (D23+: EVERYTHING re-rolls every day)** -- never cache across sets/modes. Seen: identity sizes\n  72-378 B (CRLF/LF, BOM in some sets), PDF `1.0`-`2.0`, zip entries 2-13, PE Machine (`0x014c` `0x8664` `0xaa64`\n  `0x01c0/2/4` `0x01f0` `0x0ebc` `0x5064` `0x0266`), audio under `audio-001.wav` (`pcm_s16le` `mp3` `opus` `vorbis`\n  `aac` M4A, `flac`), ELF e_machine (`0x003e` `0x0003` `0x0028` `0x002b` `0x0102` `0x0016` `0x00b7` `0x00f3`), Mach-O\n  thin (LE-32/64) or FAT 2-3 slices, Main-Class 1-4 parts, SQLite page 512-65536, EVTX 3-119 records (one chunk),\n  regf root `[A-Za-z0-9]{6,32}`, Prefetch WRAPPER flips (D26 single `MAM\\x04` Xpress-Huffman, timed plain SCCA v30),\n  PCAP classic v2.4 only (LE-us / LE-ns `4d 3c b2 a1` / BE-us `a1 b2 c3 d4`; linktype 1/101/105/147; 3-39 records,\n  snapped ones count), DISK (D28, 14 images): protective MBR `ee` + GPT rev 1.0, 512-B sectors, entries @LBA2 128x128,\n  valid CRCs, backup hdr at the last LBA, 61-582 KiB, 1-6 used entries contiguous from slot 0, starts 34-367, table\n  order == ascending, names `<word><digit>`, partitions ALL ZERO (no FS, no MBR-only/EBR/4Kn yet). Rule: decode the\n  general structure (byte order from the file, every slice/chunk/entry, follow every offset, decompress any wrapper\n  by its magic), never the D-day sample's constant.\n- **List ORDER under mutation (D23)** -- D8-D22 zips stored CD entries already sorted; D23 shuffled the CD and the GM\n  REJECTED CD order, accepted ascending sort; fat Mach-O slices ascending `0x%08x` (fat_arch order rejected). Rule:\n  `_names`/`_set`/`_targets` = sorted ascending + deduped (string sort of the emitted spelling); EXCEPT synthesis\n  (digest order) and `_sequence`/\"in order\" fields (D28: partition-TABLE order -- integers, NEVER string-sorted:\n  `[86,117]` string-sorts to `[117,86]`). Always `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"))` -- never `str()` a list.\n- **Identity member roster** (D15+) -- `evidence-note*.txt`, `evidence-note-copy*.txt`, `roster*.csv` (timed names\n  may carry `-<6hex>`; ids keep the bare stem): ids `<stem>-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,\n  text-utf8-bom-present}`; filename artifact = the container only -> map the stem by PREFIX. Sets may lack a member\n  (D25) or ask a DIFFERENT 7 of the 21 identity ids (D26+) -- answer exactly the ids each set lists.\n- **Synthesis / cross-member** (D15+) -- id `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<algo>-order` (TODAY's NN), kind `json`, norm\n  `case_insensitive`, \"Compute the full-file SHA-256 digest of each named file, then submit a compact JSON array of\n  their filenames in ascending digest order. Files: [...]\". Rule: regex `Files:\\s*(\\[.*?\\])`, hash each under the\n  ref's container, sort by hex digest -- `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo)`, get_bytes bound\n  INSIDE the per-set worker. Shape: note + re-picked kit members + TODAY's member; 4 names D15-20, FIVE D21-26, SIX\n  D27-28 (D28 TT note/png/msi/mp4/sqlite/img) -- never assume a length. The list differs between the 409 contract\n  and the live attempt AND between sets of one Mastery -- parse each set's own text. Only sha256 seen.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version, regf FileName\n  @0x30): answer from the structure the field names; `elf.*` of an `MZ` member = `none`.\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes case-insensitive; `0x`-hex `trim` only -> lowercase),\n  `enum` (`accepted_values`), `json` (compact array; `*_set`/`*_names`/`*_sequence` = a list even with ONE element).\n- **Question-text tags / nesting** -- D9 ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]` suffix, D15+ ``Inspect `<member>`. ``\n  prefix: strip, route by id + `artifact`. The asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (D7): resolve by the name after `->`;\n  OOXML/APK/JAR members ARE zips -- parse them as the member. Mastery: ONE download of `-01..-NN.zip`, refs `<set zip>\n  -> <member>`, names reused per set; download vs ref names may differ (D9) -> `lib.common.container_by_sha`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | python `zipfile` read of the member in memory (`7z l -slt` for orientation) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the member bytes; the id stem names WHICH member |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width |\n| `png.ihdr_*` | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` | of the NAMED zip: last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+10 total entries, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 (`PK\\x06\\x07` -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32) |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from cd offset: name len @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name @+46. Raw stored paths, then SORT ascending (D23: CD order REJECTED); UTF-8 if flag 0x800 else cp437 |\n| `pdf.header_version` | `head -c 16 f | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; catalog `/Version` is a diagnostic only |\n| `pe.coff_*` | `MZ` -> e_lfanew u32 @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` -> Machine u16 @+4 (any IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_*, D23 saw 7 values); OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b`/`0x20b`) |\n| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (RVA); ImageBase @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). objdump \"start address\" is the VA |\n| `pe.version_*` | `pefile` resource dir only -> `FileInfo..StringTable..entries`; id tail -> key ignoring case/`-_`. Shell: `strings -e l f.exe \\| grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n| `elf.*` (`7f 45 4c 46`) | EI_CLASS @4 (1=32, 2=64), EI_DATA @5 (1=LSB `<`, 2=MSB `>`) picks the byte order for EVERYTHING after @16: e_type u16 @16, e_machine u16 @18, e_entry @24. `xxd -s 16 -l 4 f` + `readelf -h f`. `lib.meta` fmt `elf` |\n| `macho.*` (`cf fa ed fe` LE-64, `ce fa ed fe` LE-32, `fe ed fa ce/cf` BE; fat `ca fe ba be` / fat64 `ca fe ba bf`, always BE) | thin: cputype u32 @4 (byte order from the magic). Fat: nfat_arch u32 @4, then 20-B (fat64 32-B) fat_arch {cputype, cpusubtype, offset, size, align}; Java class shares `cafebabe` (major @6 >= 45). `cpu_type_set` = JSON list `\"0x%08x\"`, deduped, SORTED ascending (D23 fat 2-3 slices). `lib.meta` fmt `macho` |\n| `apk.*` / `.apk` (`PK` + `AndroidManifest.xml` + `classes.dex`) | manifest is BINARY AXML (`03 00 08 00`): `aapt dump badging f.apk \\| head -1`; stdlib `lib/meta/apk.py manifest_attr(axml, 'manifest', 'package')`. Triage routes APKs to `$mobile-android` -- ignore it |\n| `jar.*` / `.jar/.war/.ear` (`PK` + `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`) | `unzip -p f.jar META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` (CRLF, 72-B lines, ONE-space continuations); main section up to the first blank line; `Main-Class` verbatim. Spring Boot: `Start-Class` = app. `lib/meta/prebuilt/jar.py` |\n| `sqlite.*` / `.sqlite/.db/.sqlite3` (`SQLite format 3\\0` @0) | 100-B header, BIG-endian: page size u16 @16 (`1` = 65536), write/read ver @18/@19 (2 = WAL), file change counter @24, in-header db size (pages) @28, freelist @32/@36, encoding u32 @56 (1 UTF-8, 2 UTF-16le, 3 UTF-16be), user_version @60, application_id @68, version-valid-for @92, SQLITE_VERSION_NUMBER @96. `xxd -s 16 -l 2 f`; `file f` prints the summary; `sqlite3 f 'PRAGMA page_size'`. In-window `lib/meta/prebuilt/sqlite.py` (header + stdlib sqlite_master walk + browser history) |\n| `evtx.*` / `.evtx` (`ElfFile\\0` @0, `ElfChnk\\0` @0x1000) | LE everywhere. File header: next_record_id u64 @24, chunk count u16 @42, version @36/@38 (3.2), flags u32 @120 (1 dirty, 2 full). Each 64 KiB chunk: first/last record number @8/@16, ids @24/@32, free-space offset u32 @48; records `2a 2a 00 00` from chunk+0x200, size u32 @+4, EventRecordID u64 @+8, FILETIME @+16. `record_count` = walk EVERY chunk's records up to its free offset (D24); `file f` prints chunks + next record no.; python-evtx `Evtx.Evtx` (worker-only). `lib/meta/prebuilt/evtx.py` |\n| `registry.*` / `regf.*` / `.hiv` `NTUSER.DAT` `SYSTEM` (`regf` @0) | base block 4 KiB LE: seq1/seq2 u32 @4/@8, last written FILETIME @12, ver @20/@24 (1.3), root cell off u32 @0x24 (rel. to 0x1000), bins size @0x28, FileName UTF-16 @0x30 (64 B; DECOY for the root). Cell = i32 size (neg = used) + `nk`: flags u16 @+2 (0x20 COMP_NAME -> latin-1 else UTF-16LE; 0x04 HIVE_ENTRY = root), FILETIME @+4, subkeys @+0x14, list off @+0x1c, values @+0x24, value list @+0x28, name len u16 @+0x48, name @+0x4c (offsets after the size). `hive_root_name` = root nk name verbatim (D25). `xxd -s $((0x1000+root)) -l 128`; regipy (worker-only) |\n| `prefetch.*` / `.pf` (`SCCA` @4, version u32 @0: 17/23/26/30/31; `MAM` @0 = Win10+ compressed) | `MAM` + type byte (low nibble 4 = Xpress-Huffman; 0x80 = CRC32 u32 follows), uncompressed size u32 @4, stream @8 (@12 with CRC) -> decompress FIRST. SCCA: file size u32 @12, exe name UTF-16LE @16 (60 B, NUL-terminated), path hash u32 @0x4C; run count / 8 last-run FILETIMEs / volumes per version. `.venv` `dissect.util.compression.lzxpress_huffman.decompress(b[8:])` (worker), `lib/meta/prebuilt/prefetch.py` (pure-Python, in-window) |\n| `pcap.*` / `.pcap` `.cap` (`d4 c3 b2 a1` LE-us, `4d 3c b2 a1` LE-ns, `a1 b2 c3 d4` / `a1 b2 3c 4d` BE; pcapng `0a 0d 0d 0a`) | byte order FROM THE MAGIC; 24-B global hdr: ver u16 @4/@6 (2.4), snaplen u32 @16, linktype u32 @20; records = 16-B hdr {ts_sec, ts_frac, incl_len @+8, orig_len @+12} + incl_len bytes -> `packet_count` = complete records walked (D27). pcapng: walk blocks {type u32, len u32 ... len}, SHB `0a0d0d0a` BOM `1a2b3c4d` @8 sets order per section, count EPB 6 / SPB 3 / OPB 2. `capinfos -M f` / `tshark -r f \\| wc -l` cross-check; `lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap.py` |\n| `disk.*` / `gpt.*` / `mbr.*` / `.img` `.dd` `.raw` `.001` (`55 aa` @0x1FE; `EFI PART` @512 or @4096) | protective MBR type `ee` @0x1C2 -> GPT: entry LBA u64 @hdr+72, count u32 @+80, size u32 @+84; each entry {type GUID 16, unique 16, first LBA u64 @+32, last @+40, attrs @+48, name UTF-16LE @+56}; skip all-zero type GUID; keep TABLE order (D28 `partition_start_lba_sequence` = JSON ints). No GPT -> MBR 4x16 B @0x1BE {type @+4, start u32 @+8, count @+12}, types 05/0f/85 -> walk the EBR chain (logical start = EBR LBA + rel). `sfdisk -d f.img` / `fdisk -l f.img` / `sgdisk -p f.img` / `mmls f.img` cross-check. In-window: `lib/meta/prebuilt/vbr.py` (`gpt`/`mbr` fmts) + the D28 solver's `disk_partition_starts` |\n| `dotnet.*` / Mono assembly | data dir 14 -> CLI header -> `BSJB` -> `#~` -> Module row 0 Mvid (1-based #GUID idx) -> `uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..)`. `lib/meta/dotnet.py` |\n| `msi.*` / `.msi` (OLE `d0 cf 11 e0`) | fast: `strings -n 6 x.msi \\| grep -aoE 'ProductCode\\{[0-9A-F-]{36}\\}'`; exact: CFB `!_StringPool`/`!_StringData` -> `!Property`. `olefile` in venv |\n| `lnk.*` / `.lnk` (`4c 00 00 00` + CLSID 00021401) | LinkFlags @0x14 (0x1 IDList, 0x2 LinkInfo, 0x80 Unicode); target = LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else IDList. `lib.meta.lnk:target_path` |\n| `ooxml.*` / `.docx/.xlsx/.pptx` (`PK` + `[Content_Types].xml`) | External = `TargetMode=\"External\"` in EVERY `*.rels` part; `unzip -p f.docx '*.rels' \\| grep -o 'Target=\"[^\"]*\" TargetMode=\"External\"'`; sorted |\n| `email.*` / `.eml` | `grep -ai '^message-id' f.eml`; `lib.meta.prebuilt.eml.eml_value(data, {\"field\": f})`. Values VERBATIM (Message-ID keeps `<...>`) |\n| `media.*` audio (`RIFF..WAVE`, `ID3`/`ff fb`, `OggS`, `fLaC`, `ftyp`, `1a 45 df a3`, `FORM..AIFF`) | route by MAGIC (D23 TT/Mastery: WAV, MP3, Ogg Opus, Ogg Vorbis all appeared under `audio-001.*`). WAV tag -> FFmpeg names (Conventions); Ogg: first packet `OpusHead` -> `opus`, `\\x01vorbis` -> `vorbis`. Truth: bundled `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` |\n| `media.*video*` / MP4-MOV (`....ftyp`), MKV/WebM, AVI | box walk `moov` -> first `trak` whose `mdia/hdlr` = `vide` -> `stsd` entry: w,h u16 BE @entry+32; cross-check tkhd, SPS crop. `lib.meta` fmt `media` |\n| `*-synthesis-<algo>-order` / \"Files: [...]\" in the question | parse the list from the question text, hash each member of the same container, sort by digest, compact JSON of names |\n| GUID field (`*-guid`) | spelling follows the SOURCE: stored string (MSI) verbatim braces+uppercase; binary (.NET) -> lowercase, no braces |\n| exe-extension decoy (`MZ` without `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"mislabeled\", \"embedded\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0 of the NAMED member; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(sorted(v), separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` unless the field is an order (synthesis, `_sequence`); integer lists stay ints |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids | resolve each set's container separately; see delivery layouts |\n\n## Day by day\n**Days 1-14** (one field each, all timed first try): D1 identity -> D2 `magic-prefix-hex-16` -> D3 BOM -> D4 JPEG SOFn\n`<w>x<h>` -> D5 PNG IHDR -> D6 `pdf.header_version` `x.y` -> D7 `zip.eocd_total_entries` of the INNER zip -> D8 CD names\n(compact JSON; disk order happened to be sorted) -> D9-11 one Go PE: `coff_machine_u16_hex` `0x014c`, entry RVA\n`0x%08x` (unpadded REJECTED), `version_original_filename` verbatim -> D12 `dotnet.mvid_guid` (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le)`\nlowercase, no braces) -> D13 `msi.product_code_guid` (stored WITH braces; brace-less REJECTED) -> D14 `lnk.target_path_windows`.\n\n**Days 15-27** (single = 1 new-family field; TT/Mastery = cumulative kit + synthesis): D15 `ooxml.external_relationship_\ntargets` (rels `TargetMode=\"External\"` Targets SORTED; rels order REJECTED). D16 `email.message_id` (VERBATIM with `<>`;\n2 lost: id regex -> `none`, stripped brackets). D17 `media.primary_audio_codec_name` (WAV PCM16 -> `pcm_s16le`). D18\n`media.primary_video_dimensions` (first `vide` trak stsd -> `320x180`). D19 \"Little Endian\" `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`\n(@18 in EI_DATA order -> `0x003e`). D20 \"Universal Appeal\" `macho.cpu_type_set` (THIN arm64 -> `[\"0x0100000c\"]`;\n`[\"arm64\"]` REJECTED). D21 \"Package Deal\" `apk.package_name` (binary-AXML `<manifest package=>` verbatim, NOT\n`android:label`). D22 \"Main Character Energy\" `jar.main_class` (MANIFEST.MF `Main-Class` verbatim, dotted, no\n`.class`). D23 \"Page Me Maybe\" `sqlite.page_size_bytes` (u16 BE @16, `1` = 65536; timed kit MUTATED for the first\ntime -> 1 wrong TT submit on CD-order names). D24 \"Event Horizon\" `evtx.record_count` (walk `**\\0\\0` records of EVERY\nchunk to its free-space offset u32 @48; live struct walk ~21 s). D25 \"Hive Mind\" `registry.hive_root_name` (base block\nu32 @0x24 -> nk @0x1000+off+4 -> name len u16 @+0x48, name @+0x4c, ASCII if flag 0x20; base-block FileName @0x30 =\n\"renamed\" DECOY; race MISS on fmt word, live ~17 s). D26 \"Before You Go\" `prefetch.executable_name` (single `MAM\\x04`\nXpress-Huffman -> SCCA v30, exe UTF-16LE @16 to NUL, uppercase `CMD.EXE`; timed plain SCCA; race hit ~29 s). D27 \"Packet\nLoss Prevention\" `pcap.packet_count` (24-B global hdr, then 16-B rec hdrs by incl_len @+8 to EOF; byte order + us/ns\nfrom the magic; snapped records count; prebuilt race hit ~22 s). Timed D15-17 + D19: synthesis dispatch missing ->\ngeneralize; D18, D20-22, D24-27 first try.\n\n**Day 28 — Where It All Began** (`disk.partition_start_lba_sequence`, kind `json` \"compact valid JSON array with exact\nvalues and order\", norm `trim`, id `d28-disk-001-disk-partition-start-lba-sequence`). Prompt: \"Disk images hold every\nprevious artifact family in context. Recover partition layouts, locate evidence by offset, and prove which image was\nrebuilt from an incomplete source.\" Title pun = where each partition BEGINS (start LBA) / LBA 0, where a disk begins.\n- Artifact: `metadata-day-28-evidence.zip` (606 B) -> `disk-001.img` (131 072 B = 256 sectors): protective MBR (one\n  `ee` entry), GPT header `EFI PART` @512 (rev 1.0, hdr 92 B, CRCs valid), entry array @LBA2 (128 x 128 B), backup\n  header at LBA 255; ONE used entry, Microsoft basic data, name `HUNTRESS EVIDENCE`, LBAs 34-222 -> answer `[34]`.\n  Partition bytes all zero: the flavor's \"every previous artifact family\", \"locate evidence by offset\" and \"rebuilt\n  from an incomplete source\" were NOT asked in any mode (as every day since D19).\n- Insight: GPT wins over the MBR when MBR slot 0 type is `ee` and `EFI PART` sits at LBA1; read the header's own entry\n  LBA/count/size (never hard-code 2/128/128), skip zero type-GUID entries, emit first_lba u64 @+32 per entry in TABLE\n  order as compact JSON integers (not strings, not byte offsets). MBR