{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BEeyCtk7WXixqSJERwPxPG","type":"tool_result","content":"lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_geometry.py\nlib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_media.py\n{\n \"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\",\n \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\",\n \"priority\": 1,\n \"action\": \"note\",\n \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D20 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set; D20 solver carried the dispatch forward -> timed first try; the 409 pre-fetch body listed DIFFERENT Files than the live attempt). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try. D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must start from the previous day's solve.py. D21: Files grew to FIVE names (note + panel png + managed dll + message eml + mobile-001.apk), same list in all 5 Mastery sets, order re-rolled per set -- never assume a count. D22-D23: Files = FIVE names and DIFFER between sets of one Mastery (D23: note/panel png/msi/mp4/sqlite vs note/pdf/lnk/mp4/sqlite) -- parse each set's text; still sha256-only. D24: FIVE names (note + document-001.pdf + collector-001.elf + shortcut-001.lnk + events-001.evtx), same five in all 8 Mastery sets, order re-rolled; sha256 only. D25: still sha\n\n{\n \"id\": \"disk-image-synthesis\",\n \"concept\": \"Cross-image synthesis over several disk-NNN.img members (and the D15+ digest-order synthesis carrying a large .img)\",\n \"priority\": 1,\n \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n \"detail\": \"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py: ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` with Files listing disk images: order by partition_count / first start LBA / image size / disk GUID, group images by identical partition layout (same start/end sequence), 'rebuilt image' = the one failing disk-rebuilt-integrity or whose layout matches another but whose partition contents are zero/truncated, partition-content sha256 per image (hash each partition's byte range: partition_sha256_sequence). D28 synthesis already hashed a multi-100-KB `.img` in-window; keep per-set byte caching (no id()-keyed caches, D25).\"\n}\n\n{\n \"id\": \"x509-cert\",\n \"concept\": \"X.509 subject/issuer/serial/validity/fingerprint\",\n \"priority\": 2,\n \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n \"detail\": \"fmt x509 (alias cert), fields subject_cn, issuer_cn, serial_hex, not_before_utc, not_after_utc, sha256_fingerprint, sha1_fingerprint, san_dns_names. Shares the DER walker with pe-authenticode; cryptography needs the allowlist.\"\n}\n\n{\n \"id\": \"lvm-raid-ldm\",\n \"concept\": \"Pooled / multi-disk volume metadata: LVM2, Linux md RAID, Windows LDM dynamic disks, Storage Spaces\",\n \"priority\": 3,\n \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n \"detail\": \"fmt lvm (aliases lvm2, pv): label `LABELONE` in one of the first 4 sectors (sector number u64 @8, crc @16, offset @20, `LVM2 001` @24), PV header uuid 32 chars @label+32, device size u64, metadata area -> text `vg_name { id = ... seqno = N ... logical_volumes { lv_name { segment1 { start_extent, extent_count, stripes = [\\\"pv0\\\", N] } } } }` -> vg_name, vg_uuid, seqno, pv_uuid (hyphenated 6-4-4-4-4-4-6), lv_names (sorted), extent_size, lv_segments. fmt mdraid: v0.90 superblock at end (64 KiB aligned) magic 0xa92b4efc, v1.x @0/@4096/@8 KiB: level, raid_disks, uuid, name, ctime. fmt ldm: MBR type 0x42 / GPT type 5808c8aa-7e8f-42e0-85d2-e1e90434cfb3, `PRIVHEAD` @ LBA 6 (or end of disk), disk GUID text, `TOCBLOCK`, `VMDB` -> volume names. Fields: is_dynamic, disk_group_name, volume_names.\"\n}\n\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'ssdeep'\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'ppdeep'\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tlsh'","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed430d07-8f66-4813-9978-3741f4f448f4","uuid":"781927ff-4385-4032-8e64-329edbc1727f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:41:31.807Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_geometry.py\nlib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis_media.py\n{\n \"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\",\n \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\",\n \"priority\": 1,\n \"action\": \"note\",\n \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D20 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set; D20 solver carried the dispatch forward -> timed first try; the 409 pre-fetch body listed DIFFERENT Files than the live attempt). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try. D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must star