{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZdJPCcdShuwGRwVa5Ea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LmH3PLQbacd8vwCt58LEcq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/tlog/atlas.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport json, re\np = 'reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\nt = open(p).read()\nst = json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndef built(i):\n    s = st.get('metadata-forensics:' + i, {})\n    return bool(s.get('ok')) or s.get('attempts', 0) >= 2\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a) == 1, (a[:80], t.count(a)); t = t.replace(a, b)\n\nrep(\"# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D28 post-run, 2026-10-28)\",\n    \"# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D30 post-run, 2026-10-31)\")\n\n# --- narrative: D29 + D30 paragraphs and a new Progression paragraph\na = t.index(\"Progression: D19-D22 runnable formats\"); b = t.index(\"## 1. Atlas\")\nt = t[:a] + \"\"\"**D29 \"Trust Issues\" = X.509 CERTIFICATE** (`x509.sha256_fingerprint` of one `certificate-001.pem`, 709 B, one LF\nPEM block, Ed25519; id `d29-x509-001-x509-sha256-fingerprint`, `pattern` 64 hex, `case_insensitive`). Answer = sha256 of\nthe DER (decoded base64 body). The D16-night prebuild `x509.py` HIT the race (CORRECT ~23 s, 0 wrong); TT 34 / Mastery\n442 (13 sets) first try; all 15 timed certs the same shape. Flavor (unasked): \"Certificates appear in binaries,\npackages, mail, captures, and disk images. Fingerprint each one, collapse duplicates, and identify the trust claim\nunsupported by evidence.\" -> siblings: certs inside PE Authenticode / APK signing / eml S/MIME / pcap TLS / disk\nimages, dedup by fingerprint across containers, issuer-without-matching-CA or signature that does not verify.\n**D30 \"Seeing Double\" = CORPUS RELATIONS** (`relation.identical_sha256_groups` of `cluster-001.zip`; id\n`d30-cluster-001-relation-identical-sha256-groups` -- id family `cluster`, fmt `relation`; kind `json`,\n`case_insensitive`). The FIRST field about relationships BETWEEN members rather than one member's struct. Single:\n`delivery-manifest.json` (`huntress.artifact_delivery_manifest.v1`: id/filename/path/content_type/family/producer_id/\nsize_bytes/sha256; copies `producer_id: duplicate_ref`) + 30 `artifacts/<id>.<ext>` (txt/ps1/json/png/zip) = 5 exact\ngroups x 6; answer = groups of manifest `id`s (zip paths and basenames REJECTED). Timed (15 clusters): NO manifest,\nextensionless `artifacts/<word>-NN`, shuffled CD, 19-32 members, 2-5 exact groups of 2-6, singletons, one 1-2-byte\nNEAR-duplicate shadowing each group, inner zips (one `.txt` each) of which one per group has a BAD CRC. No `relation`\nfmt in lib -> race MISS, live CORRECT ~88 s with 3 wrong (label spelling + an empty submit); TT 35 / Mastery 490 (14\nsets) first try. Flavor (unasked): \"Build a relationship map from exact identity, semantic identity, containment, and\nclaimed provenance -- then expose the fabricated cluster.\" -> the four unasked relation kinds + the fabricated\nmember/cluster are physically present in the timed bytes.\nProgression: D19-D22 runnable formats -> D23 APPLICATION DATA -> D24-D26 WINDOWS DFIR -> D27 NETWORK -> D28 DISK -> D29\nTRUST (certs) -> D30 CORPUS RELATIONS (dedup across a member set). D31 is the LAST day: a finale most plausibly asks\nthe next `relation.*` kind on a cluster (semantic identity, containment, claimed-provenance mismatch, near-duplicate /\n\"fabricated\" member, or the fabricated cluster among several) or a cross-family corpus question (inventory by magic,\nextension liars, cert dedup across containers). D31 timed kits will carry `relation.identical_sha256_groups` with\nmutations (manifest present/absent, nested dirs, md5/sha1/size variants, more near-dups). Single-member families are\nall built; the relation layer is the readiness gap.\n\n\"\"\" + t[b:]\n\n# --- atlas table rows\nrows = t.split('\\n')\nfor i, line in enumerate(rows):\n    if line.startswith('| 80 | X.509'):\n        rows[i] = line.replace('| prebuilt x509 |', '| seen D29 `x509.sha256_fingerprint` (sha256 of the DER, lowercase hex, no colons; prebuilt x509.py HIT) |', 1)\n        assert rows[i] != line\n    if line.startswith('| 84 | Cross-file'):\n        new = re.sub(r'\\| partial \\([^|]*\\) \\|', '| seen D30 `relation.identical_sha256_groups` (exact groups, rows 188+) + sha256 order D15+ |', line, 1)\n        assert new != line; rows[i] = new\n    m = re.match(r'(\\| \\d+ \\|[^|]*\\| )gap \\(([a-z0-9-]+(?:, [a-z0-9-]+)*)\\)', line)\n    if m and all(built(x) for x in m.group(2).split(', ')):\n        rows[i] = line.replace('gap (' + m.group(2) + ')', 'prebuilt (' + m.group(2) + ')', 1)\nt = '\\n'.join(rows)\nnewrows = \"\"\"| 188 | `relation.identical_sha256_groups` (corpus zip: members grouped by sha256 of real bytes, groups>=2, ids sorted inside + outside) | seen D30 (single 5x6 manifest ids; timed 2-5 groups of 2-6 extensionless basenames) | `cluster-NNN.zip`; `delivery-manifest.json` + `artifacts/*`; question \"Determine relation.<field> for cluster-001.zip\" | one `infolist()` pass, `hashlib.sha256(zf.read(zi))`; label = manifest `id` by path/filename else basename sans ext; day30 solver `d30_identical_sha256_groups` | high (D31 carry-over) |\n| 189 | Hash/size variants: `identical_{md5,sha1,sha512,size}_groups`, `unique_sha256_count`, `duplicate_group_count`, `largest_group_size`, `singleton_ids`, `member_count` | gap (relation-identical-groups-variants) | same corpus zip, other algo/aggregate word | same pass, other key | high (D31) |\n| 190 | Semantic identity: same content after normalization (BOM/CRLF/trailing ws text, canonical JSON, decoded PNG pixels w/o ancillary chunks, zip with same member bytes but other timestamps/order) | gap (relation-semantic-identity-groups) | flavor \"semantic identity\"; `semantic`/`normalized`/`canonical`/`pixel` in the field | per-family canonical key -> group | high (D31) |\n| 191 | Near-duplicate / fabricated member: 1-2-byte edit of a group's content, inner zip whose stored CRC != data CRC | gap (relation-near-duplicate-fabricated) | timed D30 clusters: one per group (`Prfference`), `BadZipFile: Bad CRC` | same-size Hamming / edit distance vs each group; CRC32 check per inner member | high (D31) |\n| 192 | Containment: which members are archives holding which (other) members, containment pairs/map, nested hashes | gap (relation-containment-map) | member magic `PK`/gzip/tar inside the cluster | open each archive member (raw read on bad CRC), hash contents, match to cluster sha256s | high (D31) |\n| 193 | Claimed provenance: manifest `sha256`/`size_bytes`/`content_type`/`family`/`producer_id` vs real bytes; `duplicate_ref` that is not a duplicate | gap (relation-claimed-provenance) | `delivery-manifest.json` / any index JSON beside the members | compare claim vs computed per id -> sorted mismatch ids | high (D31) |\n| 194 | Fabricated cluster among several `cluster-NNN.zip` (the one whose claims fail / that is a near-copy of another) | gap (relation-multi-cluster-fabricated) | >1 cluster zip in the evidence; \"expose the fabricated cluster\" | per-cluster integrity score -> the odd one | med-high (D31) |\n| 195 | Corpus inventory across every family: family by MAGIC per member, extension-vs-magic liars, per-family counts | gap (relation-corpus-family-inventory) | mixed-family corpus; \"relationship map\" | lib magic sniffer over every member | med (D31 finale) |\n| 196 | Cert dedup / unsupported trust claim across containers (D29 flavor) | gap (x509-dedup-trust-claims) | PEM/DER + PE/APK/eml/pcap carrying certs | DER sha256 per cert, issuer->subject match, signature verify (Crypto) | med |\n| 197 | Fuzzy similarity: ssdeep/CTPH, TLSH, byte-similarity percentage, most-similar pair | gap (relation-fuzzy-similarity) | `ssdeep`/`similar`/`fuzzy` in the field | pure-python CTPH (ssdeep/ppdeep/tlsh NOT installed) | low-med |\"\"\"\nanchor = t.index('\\n\\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)')\nt = t[:anchor] + '\\n' + newrows + t[anchor:]\n\n# --- recognition cues (keep <=60 lines incl. header)\nrep(\"\"\"-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE----- / 30 82 ..  X.509   cryptography x509 load_*; openssl x509 -noout -text -fingerprint -sha256\"\"\",\n\"\"\"-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE----- / 30 82 ..  X.509 (D29 `x509.sha256_fingerprint` = sha256 of the DER = decoded base64 body, hex no colons); prebuilt x509.py; openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256\ncorpus zip `cluster-NNN.zip` (+ delivery-manifest.json) RELATION (D30 `relation.identical_sha256_groups`): sha256 of REAL bytes; label = manifest `id` else extensionless basename (paths/basenames REJECTED); groups>=2, sorted in+out; manifest sha256/size/producer = CLAIMS; timed: near-dups (1-2 B edits) + bad-CRC inner zips\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"BOM ef bb bf / ff fe / fe ff -> text.*_bom_present. Byte order from the file (EI_DATA / Mach-O magic; SQLite always BE).\nMagic @0 not PK/SQLite but the magic later (PK\\\\x05\\\\x06 near EOF, `SQLite format 3\\\\0` inside) = prefixed/embedded: parse from that offset.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"BOM ef bb bf / ff fe / fe ff -> text.*_bom_present. Byte order from the file. Magic not @0 but later (PK\\\\x05\\\\x06 near EOF, `SQLite format 3\\\\0` inside) = prefixed/embedded: parse from there.\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(t)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/tlog/atlas.py; F=reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md; awk '/^## Recognition cues/{s=NR} /^## Readiness gaps/{print \"cues lines:\", NR-s}' $F; grep -c \"^| [0-9]* |.*prebuilt (\" $F","description":"Apply atlas narrative, table and cue edits"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":600,"cache_read_input_tokens":138695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":600},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed