on-identical-groups-variants\", \"`relation.*` exact-identity siblings of D30's identical_sha256_groups on a corpus zip (other hash, size, aggregates, label shapes)\", 1,\n  \"fmt relation (aliases corpus, cluster, dedup, inventory), member = a cluster zip (`cluster-NNN.zip`, optional `delivery-manifest.json` / any `*manifest*.json` / index.json). Fields: identical_sha256_groups (D30 GM-CONFIRMED: groups len>=2 of member labels, each sorted, groups sorted, compact JSON), identical_md5_groups, identical_sha1_groups, identical_sha512_groups, identical_size_groups, duplicate_groups, unique_sha256_count, duplicate_group_count, duplicate_member_count (members in groups minus one per group AND total, register both as _redundant/_in_groups), largest_group_size, singleton_ids, member_count. Label rule: manifest `id` mapped by `path` then `filename`; no manifest -> basename without extension (D30 timed `artifacts/<word>-NN`). Skip the manifest itself and directory entries; recurse into `artifacts/` subdirs; hash members as raw blobs (inner zips may hold bad-CRC entries; outer read falls back to a raw local-header read). Cache per (container sha256), never id().\"),\n (\"relation-near-duplicate-fabricated\", \"Near-duplicate / fabricated members of a corpus: a 1-2-byte edit of an exact group's content, archives whose stored CRC does not match\", 1,\n  \"fmt relation. D30 timed clusters (all 15) held, beside each exact group, ONE member equal in size differing in 1-2 bytes (`$ErrorActionPrfference`) and inner zips with one `.txt` where one copy has a stored CRC32 != data CRC (zipfile raises BadZipFile). Fields: near_duplicate_groups (group label list incl. the near-copy? register both: near_duplicate_ids = only the non-exact members, near_duplicate_pairs = [[exact_rep, near]] sorted), fabricated_ids, fabricated_member(s), crc_mismatch_ids / bad_crc_member_ids, corrupted_ids, tampered_ids, modified_copy_ids. Algorithm: for every non-grouped member, compare against each group's content: same length and Hamming distance <=4, or Levenshtein <=4 for small files (<4 KiB), or same zip member names with different data; CRC check = zlib.crc32(raw-decompressed) vs CD crc. Output sorted labels, compact JSON.\"),\n (\"relation-semantic-identity-groups\", \"Semantic identity groups: members equal after format-aware normalization (the D30 flavor's 'semantic identity')\", 1,\n  \"fmt relation. Fields: semantic_identity_groups, semantically_identical_groups, normalized_content_groups, canonical_json_groups, normalized_text_groups, pixel_identical_groups, same_content_different_hash_groups (= semantic groups that are NOT exact groups). Canonical key per family by MAGIC: text/ps1/csv -> strip UTF-8/16 BOM, decode, CRLF/CR->LF, rstrip each line, strip trailing newlines (keep case); JSON -> json.loads then dumps(sort_keys, compact); PNG -> IHDR + zlib-decompressed concatenated IDAT (ignore tEXt/tIME/iTXt and chunk order); JPEG -> bytes from SOS to EOI (ignore APPn/COM); zip -> sorted (name, sha256(data)) ignoring timestamps/extra/comment/order; gzip -> decompressed payload. Group len>=2, labels as relation-identical-groups-variants. Stdlib only (zlib, json).\"),\n (\"relation-containment-map\", \"Containment relations in a corpus: which archive members contain which other members (by hash)\", 1,\n  \"fmt relation. Fields: containment_pairs ([[container_label, contained_label_or_inner_name]] sorted), contained_ids (corpus members whose sha256 appears inside another member), container_ids, nested_member_names, nested_sha256s, max_nesting_depth, orphan_inner_members (inner contents matching no corpus member). D30 timed: inner zips each hold ONE `<word>.txt` (29-97 B) whose bytes matched NO other cluster member in sampled sets -- so also answer by inner name. Walk zip (raw-read on bad CRC: local header @offset, skip 30+n+e, inflate -15), gzip, tar; recurse <=3 levels; label inner entries `<container_label>/<inner name>` only if the field asks names.\"),\n (\"relation-claimed-provenance\", \"Claimed provenance vs evidence: delivery-manifest claims (sha256, size, content_type, family, producer_id/duplicate_ref) checked against the real bytes\", 1,\n  \"fmt relation. Manifest schema seen D30: `{schema: huntress.artifact_delivery_manifest.v1, artifacts: [{id, filename, path, content_type, family, producer_id (text_template|structured_image|structured_zip|duplicate_ref), size_bytes, sha256}]}` -- in D30 every claim was TRUE (single), timed had no manifest. Fields: claimed_hash_mismatch_ids, sha256_claim_mismatch_ids, size_claim_mismatch_ids, content_type_mismatch_ids (claim vs magic: text/plain, application/json, image/png, application/zip), family_mismatch_ids, unsupported_duplicate_ref_ids (producer duplicate_ref whose bytes match no original), missing_member_ids (claimed but absent), unlisted_member_names (present but unclaimed), provenance_mismatch_ids (union), fabricated_ids. Sorted labels, compact JSON; `[]` when all claims hold.\"),\n (\"relation-multi-cluster-fabricated\", \"Expose the fabricated cluster: several cluster-NNN.zip members, pick the one whose relations/claims do not hold\", 1,\n  \"fmt relation; question may target the evidence zip or each cluster. Fields: fabricated_cluster (filename), fabricated_cluster_id, cluster_with_claim_mismatches, clusters_sharing_content_groups, cross_cluster_identical_groups ([[\\\"cluster-001/alpha-01\\\",...]]). Score each cluster: manifest claim mismatches, near-dups, bad CRC entries, members identical to another cluster's members, timestamps in the future / identical DOS times across 'independent' sources. Return the single max-score cluster name verbatim (with .zip) and register a stem variant.\"),\n (\"relation-corpus-family-inventory\", \"Finale-style corpus inventory over every earlier family: per-member family by MAGIC, extension liars, counts\", 1,\n  \"fmt relation (aliases corpus, inventory). Fields: family_by_magic (JSON object or sorted [[label, family]] -- register both), family_counts, extension_mismatch_ids (extension vs magic), magic_family_set (sorted list of families present), members_by_family_<fam>, largest_member_id, total_bytes. Reuse lib's magic sniffer (PE/ELF/Mach-O/CFB/PK subtypes APK/JAR/OOXML/zip, PDF, PNG, JPEG, SQLite, EVTX, regf, SCCA/MAM, pcap, GPT image, PEM/DER cert, text/json/ps1). Family words = the lane's GM fmt words (email, media, registry, disk, x509, pe, elf, macho, apk, jar, sqlite, evtx, prefetch, pcap, pdf, png, jpeg, zip, ooxml, msi, lnk).\"),\n (\"x509-dedup-trust-claims\", \"D29 flavor: certificates across binaries/packages/mail/captures/disks -- fingerprint each, collapse duplicates, the trust claim unsupported by evidence\", 2,\n  \"fmt x509 (aliases cert, trust, relation). Fields: unique_fingerprint_count, duplicate_fingerprint_groups (sorted member labels per DER sha256), issuer_not_present_ids, self_signed_ids (subject==issuer AND signature verifies with own key), signature_invalid_ids, unsupported_trust_claim (member whose claimed issuer/CA has no matching subject+key in the corpus or whose signature fails), chain_order. Extract certs from PEM (multi-block), DER, PKCS7 (SignedData certificates [0]), PE Authenticode (dir 4), APK META-INF/*.RSA and v2 block, eml S/MIME parts, pcap TLS Certificate handshake. Verify Ed25519 via Crypto.Signature.eddsa, RSA via Crypto.Signature.pkcs1_15, ECDSA via Crypto.Signature.DSS (pycryptodome is in the gate allowlist). D29 single + 15 timed certs = one-block LF Ed25519 PEM.\"),\n (\"relation-fuzzy-similarity\", \"Fuzzy / similarity hashing across a corpus (ssdeep CTPH, TLSH-like, byte similarity %)\", 2,\n  \"fmt relation (alias fuzzy, ssdeep). Fields: ssdeep (per member string `blocksize:hash1:hash2`), most_similar_pair, similarity_percent, similar_groups (threshold from the question, default ssdeep compare >= 50). ssdeep/ppdeep/tlsh are NOT installed: implement ppdeep-compatible CTPH (rolling hash window 7, FNV-1 32 piecewise hash, base64 alphabet, blocksize = 3*2^k doubling until len(sig)>=32/2, compare via weighted edit distance with the 'common substring of 7' gate) in pure Python; unit-test on known vectors from the ppdeep README.\"),\n (\"relation-provenance-chain-timestamps\", \"Claimed provenance chains and timestamp relations inside a corpus (derived_from / parent links, zip DOS times vs UT extra, earliest/latest)\", 2,\n  \"fmt relation. D30 single cluster members carried `UT` (0x5455) extra fields and a manifest; timed members all shared one DOS time (2026-03-14 08:52:38). Fields: provenance_chain (parent->child order via manifest `derived_from`/`parent_id`/`source`, XMP DerivedFrom/DocumentID, OOXML/PDF ids), orphan_claim_ids (parent id not present), cycle_ids, earliest_member_id / latest_member_id, mtime_groups, dos_vs_extended_time_mismatch_ids (DOS local time vs UT/NTFS 0x000a extra), future_timestamp_ids. Sorted labels; ISO-8601 Z for times.\"),\n]\nfor gid, concept, prio, detail in NEW:\n    assert gid not in used, gid\n    gaps.append({\"id\": gid, \"concept\": concept, \"priority\": prio, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": detail})\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g: (g['priority'], 0 if g['action'] == 'note' else 1))   # stable within priority\nopen_pb = [g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action'] == 'prebuild' and not built(g['id'])]\nprint('open prebuild gaps:', len(open_pb), open_pb)\nbody = '[\\n' + ',\\n'.join('  ' + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps) + '\\n]\\n'\njson.loads(body)\npre = re.sub(r\"\\nRanking \\(D28 post-run\\).*?\\nTARGETS-style\", \"\"\"\nRanking (D30 post-run): priority 1 = plausible on D31 (the LAST day) with no extractor, or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD29 (X.509 fingerprint) was a prebuilt race HIT; D30 opened a new layer -- `relation.identical_sha256_groups`, the first\nquestion about relationships BETWEEN members of a corpus zip -- and the race MISSED (no `relation` fmt) and the live\nworker lost 3 submits on the member LABEL. Its flavor names four relation kinds 