_from / parent links, zip DOS times vs UT extra, earliest/latest)\", 2,\n  \"fmt relation. D30 single cluster members carried `UT` (0x5455) extra fields and a manifest; timed members all shared one DOS time (2026-03-14 08:52:38). Fields: provenance_chain (parent->child order via manifest `derived_from`/`parent_id`/`source`, XMP DerivedFrom/DocumentID, OOXML/PDF ids), orphan_claim_ids (parent id not present), cycle_ids, earliest_member_id / latest_member_id, mtime_groups, dos_vs_extended_time_mismatch_ids (DOS local time vs UT/NTFS 0x000a extra), future_timestamp_ids. Sorted labels; ISO-8601 Z for times.\"),\n]\nfor gid, concept, prio, detail in NEW:\n    assert gid not in used, gid\n    gaps.append({\"id\": gid, \"concept\": concept, \"priority\": prio, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": detail})\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g: (g['priority'], 0 if g['action'] == 'note' else 1))   # stable within priority\nopen_pb = [g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action'] == 'prebuild' and not built(g['id'])]\nprint('open prebuild gaps:', len(open_pb), open_pb)\nbody = '[\\n' + ',\\n'.join('  ' + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps) + '\\n]\\n'\njson.loads(body)\npre = re.sub(r\"\\nRanking \\(D28 post-run\\).*?\\nTARGETS-style\", \"\"\"\nRanking (D30 post-run): priority 1 = plausible on D31 (the LAST day) with no extractor, or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD29 (X.509 fingerprint) was a prebuilt race HIT; D30 opened a new layer -- `relation.identical_sha256_groups`, the first\nquestion about relationships BETWEEN members of a corpus zip -- and the race MISSED (no `relation` fmt) and the live\nworker lost 3 submits on the member LABEL. Its flavor names four relation kinds (exact identity, semantic identity,\ncontainment, claimed provenance) plus \"expose the fabricated cluster\", and the timed clusters already carry\nnear-duplicates and bad-CRC inner zips. So priority 1 = the relation-* family (hash/size variants, semantic groups,\nnear-duplicate/fabricated members, containment, manifest-claim mismatches, the fabricated cluster, a corpus family\ninventory). Cert dedup/trust claims, fuzzy hashing and provenance/timestamp chains at 2. The built D28 disk items\nmoved to 2 (built; the prebuild drains only unbuilt `prebuild` gaps). `x509-cert` dropped (seen D29).\nTARGETS-style\"\"\", pre, flags=re.S)\nassert 'Ranking (D30 post-run)' in pre\nt = head + '## Readiness gaps' + pre + '```json\\n' + body + '```' + post\nopen(p, 'w').write(t)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/tlog/gaps.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re,json\nt=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md').read()\nm=re.search(r\"## Readiness gaps.*?```json\\s*(.*?)```\", t, re.S); g=json.loads(m.group(1))\nprint(len(g), all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g), len({x['id'] for x in g}))\nEOF","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps JSON block"}}}
